  "strategy": [
    "The May 2026 paper has 15 questions: five 5-mark parts in Q1, then two 10-mark parts under each of Q2 to Q6. Q1 parts come from different modules, so cover all six.",
    "Word sense disambiguation and NLP applications (machine translation, summarization, question answering) appear in all 9 exam papers. Dictionary-based WSD with Lesk is in 7 of 9, so learn it before the other WSD methods.",
    "The Porter stemmer is a 10-marker in 8 of the 9 papers, including all three own-branch papers (December 2024, May 2025, May 2026). One well-learned answer is close to certain marks.",
    "HMM, MaxEnt and CRF questions appear in 8 of 9 papers, a bigram-probability corpus numerical in 4 and an HMM probability numerical in 4. Practise one of each.",
    "CYK, shift-reduce, PCFG, top-down vs bottom-up and Good-Turing carry the note 'not in the CSE (AI&ML) syllabus' and were asked only in CE papers. Skip them if you follow that syllabus."
  ]
